        "x1": 0.47276633986928107,
        "y1": 0.8745795454545454
      },
      "text": "Fig. 10: Sensing profile for a target beyond the ISI-free range.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07679738562091504,
        "y0": 0.8859431818181818,
        "x1": 0.4934640522875817,
        "y1": 0.9473901515151515
      },
      "text": "When multiple targets coexist; as shown in Fig. 11(a), the resultant ISI and ICI from targets beyond the ISI-free range adds up; which may lift the noise level up. However; according to (39), the total ISIICI resultant by all the 6 targets beyond the ISI-free distance is only ~98dBm, which slightly lifts the noise level from ~87.17dBm to ~86.83dBm. In general, when the number of subcarriers is sufficiently large, the impact of ISI and ICI caused by CP limitation is negligible for sensing. According to the   specifications   in 5G NR, the   bandwidth when the simulation reduces from 2048 to 288 in Fig. 11(b), the interference power will increase to ~97.86dBm, which is still negligible as compared with the noise level.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
